From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:42:33 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: gpio: apple,smc-gpio: Add apple,output-templates

The SMC sets some lines, such as resets it sequences itself, through a
function value instead of its output command: the J713's ADT gives the
multi-touch AFE reset as a 4-byte write of 0x10000 to gP1c, with the
argument in the low bits. The output command on that line does not
reset the AFE. Describe such lines and their templates.

Signed-off-by: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/gpio/apple,smc-gpio.yaml     | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpio/apple,smc-gpio.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpio/apple,smc-gpio.yaml
index 42b1bc0a10c9..d9308dea0232 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpio/apple,smc-gpio.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpio/apple,smc-gpio.yaml
@@ -21,6 +21,18 @@ properties:
   '#gpio-cells':
     const: 2
 
+  apple,output-templates:
+    description:
+      Lines that the SMC sets through a function value rather than its output
+      command, as some resets need. Setting such a line writes its template
+      with the line's value in the low 16 bits.
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32-matrix
+    items:
+      items:
+        - description: GPIO line
+          maximum: 63
+        - description: Template, with the low 16 bits clear
+
 required:
   - compatible
   - gpio-controller
